Subject: [PATCH 5/5] LOCAL ONLY: refuse raw register writes outside the algorithm block

NOT for upstream as written, because it assumes the hcfpga register layout. LITEPCIE_IOCTL_REG checks
only that an address lies inside BAR0, and BAR0 also holds the SoC reset and the DMA descriptor
tables. Any account that can open /dev/litepcie* could write a descriptor with an arbitrary bus
address and have the DMA engine read or write any physical memory, which is a kernel read and write
primitive on a host without a translating IOMMU. A write to the SoC reset kills the PCIe endpoint,
and on an AMD host the next read resets the machine, as described in patch 3.

hashcat writes only the algorithm block through this ioctl, below CSR_CTRL_BASE. Writes at or above
it are now refused with EPERM, and the DMA engine is programmed only through the driver's own ioctls
and buffers. Reads stay allowed, because the bridge reads the link status and the temperature there.

Signed-off-by: See docs/credits.txt

--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -1081,6 +1081,19 @@
 			break;
 		}
 
+#ifdef CSR_CTRL_BASE
+		/* LOCAL: raw writes are limited to the algorithm block, which is
+		 * all hashcat writes through this ioctl. From CSR_CTRL_BASE up are
+		 * the SoC reset and the DMA descriptor tables. A raw write there
+		 * lets any account that can open the node reset the host or point
+		 * the DMA engine at arbitrary physical memory. Reads stay allowed.
+		 */
+		if (m.is_write && m.addr >= CSR_CTRL_BASE) {
+			ret = -EPERM;
+			break;
+		}
+#endif
+
 		if (m.is_write)
 			litepcie_writel(dev, m.addr, m.val);
 		else
